controlled data and it passed: 1,439 ordered requests per engine, zero request errors,
and every response matched once two known render artifacts were set aside. It is not
finished. The hosted Bunny half has not been run, no triage ruling exists for any
difference yet, and the final run still has to happen on the final code with a serving
artifact bound to that code. One difference is already measured and still open: in
seven write cases the port's notification mail carries an extra redirect parameter that
Ruby does not send, and the read-only request list cannot see it.

